            // Identity
            B.q("sa-m5-5", "sa-identity", "Staff already carry smart cards with X.509 certificates from the company's own certificate authority, and should use them to sign in to Microsoft Entra ID, without AD FS. What do you recommend?", listOf("Microsoft Entra certificate-based authentication", "Keep AD FS just for smart cards", "SMS sign-in", "Password hash synchronization only"), setOf(0), "Microsoft Entra certificate-based authentication lets users sign in with X.509 certificates, such as those on smart cards, directly against Entra ID. It is phishing-resistant and needs no federation server.",
